WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:04.560
As we buckle in for the forthcoming premiere
of Avengers: Endgame, there are a lot of moving

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:09.500
parts to keep track of: after all, we're talking
about 21 movies over about a decade.

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:13.540
It's the perfect time to look back over the
history of the Marvel Cinematic Universe and

00:00:13.550 --> 00:00:17.710
go over everything fans should have in mind
before scanning that ticket, ordering some

00:00:17.710 --> 00:00:21.280
popcorn, and settling in for Marvel's cinematic
event of the year.

00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:24.600
A quick word of warning: spoilers for Captain
Marvel ahead!

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:29.860
One consistent thread throughout many of the
MCU's films before Infinity War has been the

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:31.700
impending approach of Thanos.

00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:36.060
We saw elements of the Mad Titan all the way
back in the first Avengers movie, when we

00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:38.580
caught a shot of his grinning face in the
mid-credits scene.

00:00:39.090 --> 00:00:43.400
He played a role in the Guardians of the Galaxy
franchise as well and reappeared at the end

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:47.520
of Avengers: Age of Ultron when he donned
an Infinity Gauntlet and uttered the famous

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:48.020
line:

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:49.080
"Fine.

00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:52.540
I'll do it myself."

00:00:53.020 --> 00:00:57.280
Infinity War brought Thanos crashing into
the primary narrative, as the big purple one

00:00:57.280 --> 00:01:00.300
traipsed around the galaxy, gathering up the
Infinity Stones.

00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:04.839
He already had the Power Stone when the film
began, and his encounter with Thor and the

00:01:04.839 --> 00:01:09.649
surviving Asgardians in Infinity War's opening
moments left him with the Tesseract, which

00:01:09.649 --> 00:01:10.760
hid the Space Stone.

00:01:11.030 --> 00:01:15.260
He proceeded from there to get the Reality
Stone on Knowhere, the Soul Stone on Vormir

00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:19.729
after sacrificing Gamora, and the Time Stone
after Doctor Strange surrendered it to him

00:01:19.729 --> 00:01:20.220
on Titan.

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:25.200
Last but not least, he headed to Wakanda,
where he plucked the Mind Stone out of Vision's

00:01:25.209 --> 00:01:29.750
forehead, completed his gauntlet, and snapped
his fingers, wiping out half of the life in

00:01:29.750 --> 00:01:32.260
the universe in what has been dubbed "the
Decimation."

00:01:33.160 --> 00:01:37.560
Over time, the Avengers lineup has come to
include characters like War Machine, Scarlet

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:42.200
Witch, Vision, Falcon, and Spider-Man, but
it all started with the Big Six.

00:01:42.469 --> 00:01:47.520
As The Avengers played out, a nucleus of heroes
slowly came together, including Hulk, Iron

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:50.940
Man, Hawkeye, Thor, Black Widow, and Captain
America.

00:01:51.469 --> 00:01:56.779
2016's Civil War saw the group split, with
Cap, Hawkeye, and Black Widow heading off

00:01:56.780 --> 00:01:58.460
into exile in the aftermath.

00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:03.240
While almost everyone was involved in Infinity
War, the heroes weren't fully unified throughout

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:03.740
the film.

00:02:04.289 --> 00:02:08.620
But as savvy fans quickly realized, as the
dust from the Decimation settled, not one

00:02:08.620 --> 00:02:10.560
of the original Avengers had been dusted.

00:02:10.820 --> 00:02:15.380
Half of the universe's population may be gone,
but it sure is convenient that all six of

00:02:15.380 --> 00:02:18.000
the original Avengers survived the dusting…
isn't it?

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:22.900
It seems natural that Endgame would pick up
the storyline where Infinity War left off,

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:27.900
just after Thanos' Decimation swept half of
the life in the universe into the dustbin.

00:02:28.140 --> 00:02:30.320
That actually might not be the case, however.

00:02:30.780 --> 00:02:35.240
For quite a while now the timing of Endgame
within the MCU's greater timeline has been

00:02:35.240 --> 00:02:37.460
mysteriously impossible to pin down.

00:02:38.150 --> 00:02:41.940
Some rumors suggest it'll start with as much
as a five-year jump into the future.

00:02:41.960 --> 00:02:42.760
So which is it?

00:02:42.980 --> 00:02:47.360
Well, as each new trailer has hit, it seems
the answer might be "both."

00:02:47.880 --> 00:02:49.080
The key to it all: the hair.

00:02:49.780 --> 00:02:54.230
In the first Endgame teaser, Natasha Romanoff
is seen with the blonde, short hair that she

00:02:54.230 --> 00:02:55.860
sported throughout Infinity War.

00:02:56.290 --> 00:03:00.580
In a more recent Endgame trailer, though,
she's shown repeatedly with red hair past

00:03:00.599 --> 00:03:04.650
her shoulders, with wisps of blonde on the
end, indicating that she's been growing it

00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:05.680
out for some time.

00:03:06.260 --> 00:03:10.180
However it all pieces together, it's pretty
certain that we're in for some kind of time

00:03:10.180 --> 00:03:13.160
jump, or jumps, either before or throughout
the film.

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:17.700
If you haven't seen Ant-Man and the Wasp yet,
you really ought to before you see Endgame,

00:03:17.700 --> 00:03:20.580
if not just for the fun of it all, then for
the Quantum Realm.

00:03:21.129 --> 00:03:25.780
While we caught a glimpse of in the first
Ant-Man, the sequel dove headlong into exploring

00:03:25.780 --> 00:03:30.390
that other-worldly dimension as the team tried
their hardest to get Janet van Dyne out after

00:03:30.390 --> 00:03:31.540
decades trapped there.

00:03:32.209 --> 00:03:36.600
Hank and Hope created a Quantum device that,
by the end of the movie, facilitated Quantum

00:03:36.600 --> 00:03:38.300
Realm travel quite easily.

00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:43.060
This led to the now super-important lines
from original Wasp Janet Van Dyne:

00:03:43.060 --> 00:03:45.340
"And don't get sucked into a time vortex.

00:03:45.340 --> 00:03:47.250
We won't be able to save you."

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:52.040
That, of course, is a huge hint that there
will be some time traveling shenanigans in

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:52.540
Endgame.

00:03:53.340 --> 00:03:57.190
We don't know how Scott Lang makes his way
out of the Quantum Realm, but it certainly

00:03:57.190 --> 00:04:01.420
appears that the super-powerful microverse
is going to feature fairly heavily in Endgame.

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:06.600
In fact, Hank Pym actor Michael Douglas even
went so far as to say it's "the key" to Phase

00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:07.100
4.

00:04:07.620 --> 00:04:11.560
Endgame promises to be a heck of a long movie
and the kind of watching experience that's

00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:16.420
better off not interrupted by sudden attempts
to remember why a character is or isn't in

00:04:16.420 --> 00:04:17.340
a certain location.

00:04:17.820 --> 00:04:22.440
So let's recap where some of our beloved heroes,
at least those who weren't snapped, were when

00:04:22.440 --> 00:04:23.800
Infinity War wrapped up.

00:04:24.640 --> 00:04:28.720
Tony Stark and Nebula are the only survivors
of the snap still stranded on Titan.

00:04:29.160 --> 00:04:33.360
However, the first Endgame trailer reminded
us that the pair have access to the Guardians

00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:35.100
of the Galaxy's ship, the Benatar.

00:04:35.750 --> 00:04:39.380
While their trip home may be fraught with
peril, another trailer seems to indicate that

00:04:39.380 --> 00:04:42.660
a reunion is in order for Stark, Nebula, and
the gang on Earth.

00:04:42.990 --> 00:04:48.080
Meanwhile, Cap, Black Widow, Banner, Thor,
Okoye, Rocket, and Rhodey were

00:04:48.080 --> 00:04:52.200
all present at the fight in Wakanda as the
dust of their allies settled around them.

00:04:52.840 --> 00:04:56.200
Once again, the trailers seem to hint that
at least some of them will have headed back

00:04:56.200 --> 00:04:58.120
to the Avengers HQ in the interim.

00:04:58.520 --> 00:05:02.620
Scott Lang was literally trapped in the Quantum
Realm by the snap, with the trailers showing

00:05:02.620 --> 00:05:04.940
that he will, somehow, make his way out alive.

00:05:05.340 --> 00:05:08.080
Finally, Carol Danvers was away when the snap
occurred.

00:05:08.760 --> 00:05:12.620
But her own film's mid-credits scene shows
that she'll respond to Nick Fury's pager by

00:05:12.620 --> 00:05:13.680
showing up on Earth again.

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:19.920
One sleeper character in all of this is Tony's
fiancee and Stark Industries CEO Pepper Potts.

00:05:20.440 --> 00:05:24.670
While she did play a brief role in Infinity
War, Potts' presence was chiefly marked by

00:05:24.670 --> 00:05:29.180
her repeated insistence that Stark should
hang up his suit for good, followed by a brief,

00:05:29.180 --> 00:05:32.820
alarming phone call as Tony sped away into
space on the flying donut.

00:05:33.170 --> 00:05:36.940
But while Pep may have dropped off the radar
at that point, it hardly means she's sitting

00:05:36.940 --> 00:05:38.670
out of Endgame.

00:05:38.670 --> 00:05:43.400
Potts has played a quietly pivotal role in
Tony Stark's life, providing stability, direction,

00:05:43.400 --> 00:05:45.460
and wisdom, and giving him a reason to fight.

00:05:45.920 --> 00:05:50.120
There's a good chance she'll actually play
a bigger role than anyone might anticipate.

00:05:50.380 --> 00:05:54.980
Gwyneth Paltrow has announced that Endgame
will be her last MCU performance, at least

00:05:54.990 --> 00:05:59.460
for the time being, which makes this film
an ideal spot to drop Potts into the thick

00:05:59.460 --> 00:06:04.240
of things, maybe even in the form of her own
comic book superhero persona, Rescue.

00:06:04.850 --> 00:06:09.180
The sight of Potts saving Stark for a second
time after she armored up in Iron Man 3 would

00:06:09.180 --> 00:06:10.960
be about as sweet as it gets.

00:06:11.500 --> 00:06:15.340
Of course, if we're going to cover Stark and
Potts, it's important to go into Endgame with

00:06:15.340 --> 00:06:18.280
one other character on our minds: Steve Rogers.

00:06:18.680 --> 00:06:22.900
Captain America has been an integral presence
throughout the MCU since he first donned that

00:06:22.900 --> 00:06:25.980
shield and ran out into the battlefields of
World War II.

00:06:26.440 --> 00:06:31.310
Along with Stark, the second Endgame trailer
focuses heavily on Cap, showing multiple scenes

00:06:31.310 --> 00:06:34.300
of his past films while featuring his plan
to do whatever it takes.

00:06:34.300 --> 00:06:35.100
"Whatever it takes."

00:06:35.440 --> 00:06:36.480
"Whatever it takes."

00:06:39.960 --> 00:06:40.760
"Whatever it takes."

00:06:43.980 --> 00:06:47.840
The fact that he kicks off the team's mantra
isn't surprising, coming from the man that

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:50.680
has served as the Avengers' moral compass
for years.

00:06:51.020 --> 00:06:53.980
Rogers' story arc has been dramatic, to say
the least.

00:06:54.190 --> 00:06:57.840
He started out desperate to prove himself,
ended up saving the world from the threat

00:06:57.840 --> 00:07:01.640
of Red Skull, and then survived an icy nap
for decades.

00:07:01.840 --> 00:07:06.320
Since then, he's unofficially co-led the Avengers
with Stark, with his storyline feeling like

00:07:06.320 --> 00:07:09.020
it's been building towards something big for
quite a while.

00:07:09.720 --> 00:07:14.640
Cap actor Chris Evans even caused a stir in
late 2018 when he tweeted what appeared to

00:07:14.640 --> 00:07:17.020
be an emotional farewell to the MCU.

00:07:17.540 --> 00:07:21.700
While the tweet was excused away, it's been
hard to shake the uncomfortable feeling that

00:07:21.720 --> 00:07:24.720
Cap could be in for a tragic story arc in
Endgame.

00:07:24.960 --> 00:07:27.060
It's something worth preparing for, at least.

00:07:27.960 --> 00:07:32.100
It's impossible to talk about Infinity War
without addressing the conspicuous absence

00:07:32.100 --> 00:07:32.680
of the Hulk.

00:07:33.460 --> 00:07:37.810
As the film opened, Hulk was coming off a
galaxy-wide romp that saw him as a gladiator

00:07:37.810 --> 00:07:43.090
hero on Sakaar, followed by a battle on Asgard
that saw him recklessly tackle a giant wolf

00:07:43.090 --> 00:07:45.940
and smack an apocalyptic fire demon in the
face.

00:07:46.290 --> 00:07:50.800
The guy was on a roll, but it only took Thanos
a few seconds and a handful of well-placed

00:07:50.800 --> 00:07:54.200
punches to get the Green Machine to go down
like a sack of potatoes.

00:07:54.500 --> 00:07:59.000
Heimdall literally gave his life to save the
Emerald Giant, yet the rest of the film hardly

00:07:59.000 --> 00:08:01.520
showcased a Hulk that was thankful in the
least.

00:08:01.870 --> 00:08:06.340
In the battle with Ebony Maw in New York followed
by the big fight in Wakanda, Hulk refused

00:08:06.340 --> 00:08:10.920
to come out to help, leaving the mild-mannered
Banner to do his best with a Hulkbuster suit.

00:08:11.210 --> 00:08:15.680
While Hulk may have appeared scared, co-director
Joe Russo explained that he's simply, quote,

00:08:15.680 --> 00:08:17.860
"tired of playing hero to Bruce Banner."

00:08:18.280 --> 00:08:22.600
Actor Mark Ruffalo has also gone on record
claiming that the two characters are "headed

00:08:22.600 --> 00:08:26.880
for a showdown," adding in another interview
that the Hulk has been going through a three-movie

00:08:26.880 --> 00:08:28.760
story of his own that will end with Endgame.

00:08:29.200 --> 00:08:33.180
However it plays out, we should expect to
see some green fireworks at some point.

00:08:40.360 --> 00:08:44.700
Thor has been an MCU staple for a long time,
and the character has definitely been put

00:08:44.700 --> 00:08:45.380
through the wringer.

00:08:45.680 --> 00:08:50.960
While he started out as a jolly exile, smashing
coffee cups and asking to ride around on pets,

00:08:50.960 --> 00:08:54.640
Thor has slowly been shaped into a real leader
through tragedy and grief.

00:08:55.120 --> 00:08:58.800
He's lost his entire family, as well as his
home and most of his people.

00:08:59.240 --> 00:09:03.640
And to top it all off, he also lost his mighty
hammer when his sister crushed it to bits.

00:09:04.040 --> 00:09:06.000
"You have no idea what's possible."

00:09:11.520 --> 00:09:14.000
To sum it up, Thor has gone through a lot.

00:09:14.180 --> 00:09:18.760
He put that grief and anger to good use, spending
the greater part of Infinity War off making

00:09:18.770 --> 00:09:22.950
his new weapon, Stormbreaker, and when he
arrived in Wakanda he was swift to put it

00:09:22.950 --> 00:09:27.610
to use: in fact, he ended up being the only
Avenger who dealt what looked to be a truly

00:09:27.610 --> 00:09:29.260
deadly blow to the Mad Titan.

00:09:29.740 --> 00:09:31.740
Of course, he should have gone for the head.

00:09:32.200 --> 00:09:36.640
That attack worked mainly because Thor had
the element of surprise, when he and Thanos

00:09:36.640 --> 00:09:42.000
meet again, things could go very differently…
and possibly because, thanks to time travel,

00:09:42.000 --> 00:09:46.400
he might be doing things he already did in
Infinity War differently… maybe this time

00:09:46.400 --> 00:09:50.220
he will have gone for the head, finally putting
Thanos's advice to good use.

00:09:51.020 --> 00:09:54.620
Another character glaringly absent from Infinity
War was Clint Barton.

00:09:54.900 --> 00:09:58.780
Everyone's favorite sharpshooter sat out the
fight with Thanos after the events of Captain

00:09:58.780 --> 00:10:01.540
America: Civil War left him under house arrest.

00:10:01.800 --> 00:10:06.460
But while Hawkeye may not have quite the same
power level in a fight as Hulk or Thor, his

00:10:06.460 --> 00:10:09.050
presence was seriously missed by fans of the
MCU.

00:10:09.260 --> 00:10:13.100
Sure, he may not have been able to turn the
tide of the battle in Wakanda, but unlike

00:10:13.100 --> 00:10:16.440
Thor, he definitely would've gone for the
head once Thanos showed up.

00:10:16.940 --> 00:10:20.720
The trailers for Endgame strongly suggest
that Barton will make his return with the

00:10:20.720 --> 00:10:24.800
new persona of Ronin, a name he briefly adopted
in the comics.

00:10:25.029 --> 00:10:28.940
The new Barton looks meaner than ever, with
an ferocious-looking mohawk and an apparent

00:10:28.950 --> 00:10:33.610
thirst for vengeance, fueled by the potential
loss of all or at least part of his family

00:10:33.610 --> 00:10:34.780
in Thanos' Decimation.

00:10:35.680 --> 00:10:39.260
Another character to remember heading into
Endgame is Carol Danvers.

00:10:39.520 --> 00:10:44.900
The spacefaring superhero electrified audiences
when she made her debut in March 2019.

00:10:45.240 --> 00:10:49.330
Up until then, Captain Marvel had only been
hinted at during the end credits scene from

00:10:49.330 --> 00:10:53.770
Infinity War, with her red, blue, and gold
insignia showing up in Nick Fury's special

00:10:53.770 --> 00:10:54.260
pager.

00:10:54.840 --> 00:10:59.460
The tease sparked much fan speculation over
how her eventual arrival might turn the tables

00:10:59.460 --> 00:11:01.420
on Thanos in the aftermath of the snap.

00:11:02.180 --> 00:11:07.160
As Captain Marvel's solo movie demonstrates,
this war-fighter is incredibly powerful, capable

00:11:07.160 --> 00:11:10.660
of taking on an entire fleet of spaceships
and warheads single-handedly.

00:11:11.600 --> 00:11:15.580
The end credits scene of her film reveals
that Captain Marvel will indeed find her way

00:11:15.580 --> 00:11:20.830
back to Earth to answer Fury's call, so now
the major question going into Endgame is how

00:11:20.830 --> 00:11:24.740
she'll help bring down Thanos and reverse
the effects of the Decimation.

00:11:25.170 --> 00:11:29.820
She probably won't be able to pull it off
alone, but as the strongest hero in the MCU,

00:11:29.820 --> 00:11:31.560
she'll probably be a pretty big help.

00:11:32.320 --> 00:11:36.280
The end of Infinity War showed us a brief
epilogue of Thanos beginning what appeared

00:11:36.280 --> 00:11:38.860
to be a new life as a semi-retired farmer.

00:11:39.410 --> 00:11:44.020
The Mad Titan is seen in a small hut, watching
the sun rise on what he perhaps imagines to

00:11:44.020 --> 00:11:45.360
be a grateful universe.

00:11:45.740 --> 00:11:49.880
Of course, we all know Endgame will show that
the universe really isn't that grateful for

00:11:49.880 --> 00:11:51.100
his actions after all.

00:11:51.440 --> 00:11:55.360
But just because they want vengeance doesn't
mean our intrepid heroes will be able to just

00:11:55.360 --> 00:11:57.960
pop over and pay the Mad Titan a visit…
right?

00:11:58.220 --> 00:12:00.720
Where is Thanos at the end of Infinity War,
anyway?

00:12:01.500 --> 00:12:05.460
It seems that the Titan has chosen a location
that the Russo brothers have dubbed "Titan

00:12:05.460 --> 00:12:05.960
II."

00:12:06.360 --> 00:12:10.540
The trailers have shown more of his retirement,
with scenes of Thanos walking his fields and

00:12:10.600 --> 00:12:12.700
a shot of his armor hung up like a scarecrow.

00:12:13.190 --> 00:12:17.420
In addition, a purported leak for the movie
has hinted that Nebula might have knowledge

00:12:17.420 --> 00:12:21.280
of a place that her father was preparing to
retire to after his work was done.

00:12:22.050 --> 00:12:26.180
Wherever the so-called Titan II is, we can
assume that Thanos won't be spending time

00:12:26.180 --> 00:12:28.500
there in peaceful solitude for very long.

00:12:29.240 --> 00:12:33.640
One special element of Infinity War was the
crossover of the Guardians of the Galaxy with

00:12:33.640 --> 00:12:34.960
the rest of the MCU.

00:12:35.350 --> 00:12:39.380
The scene where Iron Man, Spider-Man, and
Doctor Strange bump into Star-Lord and the

00:12:39.390 --> 00:12:44.440
gang on Titan was well worth the wait, feeling
more so than usual like seeing a crossover

00:12:44.440 --> 00:12:46.000
comic book story come to life.

00:12:46.740 --> 00:12:48.320
"I'm gonna ask you this one time.

00:12:49.540 --> 00:12:50.200
Where is Gamora?"

00:12:50.460 --> 00:12:51.460
"I'll do you one better.

00:12:51.640 --> 00:12:52.640
Who's Gamora?"

00:12:52.720 --> 00:12:55.500
"I'll do you one better: Why is Gamora?"

00:12:55.660 --> 00:12:59.120
The Guardians ended up playing fairly pivotal
roles throughout the film, too.

00:12:59.660 --> 00:13:03.820
Rocket helped Thor build his new weapon, while
Groot literally lent a hand in order to give

00:13:03.840 --> 00:13:04.860
the ax a handle.

00:13:05.280 --> 00:13:09.779
Gamora tried her best to stop her adopted
father, but ultimately ended up leading him

00:13:09.780 --> 00:13:11.760
to the Soul Stone, and losing her life.

00:13:12.300 --> 00:13:16.290
On Titan, Mantis played a critical role in
the battle by putting Thanos to sleep at a

00:13:16.290 --> 00:13:17.420
crucial moment.

00:13:17.620 --> 00:13:19.660
Who would have thought she'd be that useful
in a fight?

00:13:20.290 --> 00:13:23.540
But if you're going to highlight the heroics,
then you've also got to balance it out with

00:13:23.540 --> 00:13:28.190
one of the most boneheaded moves of the whole
film: Star-Lord's doomed assault on Thanos

00:13:28.190 --> 00:13:31.360
just when his teammates were about to get
the gauntlet off his hand.

00:13:31.820 --> 00:13:35.800
From there, things went south pretty quickly,
with the Decimation leaving everyone on the

00:13:35.800 --> 00:13:38.900
team except Rocket and Nebula a pile of ashes.

00:13:39.240 --> 00:13:43.080
While Rocket's role in Endgame will likely
involve helping the Earthbound heroes reach

00:13:43.080 --> 00:13:48.520
Thanos, Nebula's role might be even more interesting,
as she was a key player in defeating Thanos

00:13:48.520 --> 00:13:49.360
in the comics.

00:13:49.980 --> 00:13:53.320
It's hard to talk about Infinity War without
bringing up Doctor Strange.

00:13:53.640 --> 00:13:59.460
Since his entrance into the MCU in 2016, Strange
has played a major role in the series' greater

00:13:59.460 --> 00:14:00.120
storyline.

00:14:00.460 --> 00:14:04.840
In Thor: Ragnarok, he helped Thor and Loki
find Odin; in Infinity War, he pushed the

00:14:04.840 --> 00:14:06.920
plot forward in a few major ways.

00:14:07.280 --> 00:14:11.480
For one thing, the Master of the Mystic Arts
was also the keeper of the Time Stone.

00:14:11.640 --> 00:14:16.560
This made him a prime target on Thanos' hit
list, with Ebony Maw coming to New York specifically

00:14:16.560 --> 00:14:17.540
to retrieve it.

00:14:18.089 --> 00:14:24.240
It was Strange who used his powers to peer
ahead at 14,000,605 future scenarios, only

00:14:24.240 --> 00:14:26.540
one of which ended in Thanos' defeat.

00:14:27.029 --> 00:14:31.420
He played a courageous role in the physical
fight against Thanos, too, but his real strategy

00:14:31.430 --> 00:14:36.100
started coming together when he unexpectedly
surrendered the stone in exchange for Tony

00:14:36.100 --> 00:14:36.620
Stark's life.

00:14:37.320 --> 00:14:41.480
While Strange may have faded away in the snap
like so many others, he was pretty clearly

00:14:41.480 --> 00:14:46.540
setting things up for the "endgame" he predicted,
leaving the surviving heroes in the one timeline

00:14:46.540 --> 00:14:48.120
where there's any hope for victory.

00:14:48.680 --> 00:14:53.140
It's also been noted that Tilda Swinton will
be returning for Endgame as the Ancient One,

00:14:53.140 --> 00:14:54.380
Strange's deceased mentor.

00:14:54.700 --> 00:14:58.300
How she'll fit into the picture remains a
mystery, but the fact that she's showing up

00:14:58.300 --> 00:15:02.520
from beyond the grave probably speaks to the
good Doctor's importance to the storyline.

00:15:03.180 --> 00:15:07.540
There's no doubt that Endgame will be an epic
capstone to the first three phases of the

00:15:07.540 --> 00:15:11.180
MCU, and Marvel seems to be just getting ramped
up at this point.

00:15:11.640 --> 00:15:16.360
After Endgame closes out the story arc for
the Infinity Stones saga, a whole new chapter

00:15:16.360 --> 00:15:18.220
begins, and it's loaded with potential.

00:15:18.910 --> 00:15:23.300
Captain Marvel's arrival bodes well for the
Avengers, as Brie Larson is reportedly signed

00:15:23.300 --> 00:15:28.020
on for seven features and seems poised to
be the face of the MCU for quite a while.

00:15:28.300 --> 00:15:32.920
In addition, the Disney/Fox merger promises
to add characters like the Fantastic Four,

00:15:32.920 --> 00:15:38.090
the Silver Surfer, X-Men, and Deadpool to
the MCU while also opening the doors for villains

00:15:38.090 --> 00:15:40.040
like Magneto and Doctor Doom.

00:15:40.460 --> 00:15:44.471
Sequels for the Black Panther and Doctor Strange
franchises are in the works as well, while

00:15:44.471 --> 00:15:49.190
Disney's rehiring of James Gunn has put the
Guardians of the Galaxy series back in fans'

00:15:49.190 --> 00:15:50.180
good graces.

00:15:50.550 --> 00:15:54.920
So while Endgame is likely to be the last
go-around for a few beloved characters and

00:15:54.930 --> 00:15:58.790
storylines, there's plenty more being built
for the next chapters in a universe that's

00:15:58.790 --> 00:16:00.440
getting bigger all the time.

